  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light is incident at an angle of <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>60</mn></mrow> <mo>&#8728;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> on one face of a prism of angle <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>30</mn></mrow> <mo>&#8728;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math>. The emergent ray of light makes an angle of <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mn>30</mn></mrow> <mo>&#8728;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> with incident ray. The angle made by the emergent ray with second face of prism will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mn>0</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mn>45</mn><mo>°</mo></mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Incidence angle on one face of a prism, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Angle of the prism, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>,<p>the mergent ray&nbsp;that makes an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with incident ray. We know, deviation angle,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#948;</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Angle&nbsp;between the&nbsp;incident ray and emergent ray<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#948;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. So, the angle with the face,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow> </math>."
  }
}